1078	  /* RevealChangeText — a slot that slides its content out from one edge and
1079	   * tucks it back under whatever follows. WIDTH is the animated property, not a
1080	   * transform: the point is that the row around it re-centres and re-flows as
1081	   * the slot opens and closes, which a transform (no layout effect) cannot do.
1082	   *
1083	   * `justify-content` is what picks the edge. Pinning the content's RIGHT edge
1084	   * (the default) means narrowing the box eats the content from the LEFT — it
1085	   * tucks under the next element and reveals back out from that same seam.
1086	   *
